      "title": "VQE Molecular Ground-State Energy",
      "description": "The Variational Quantum Eigensolver (VQE) is a hybrid quantum-classical algorithm for finding the ground-state energy of molecules. This application uses the hydrogen molecule (H2) as an example, constructing the molecular Hamiltonian under the STO-3G basis set, and searching for the ground-state energy through a hardware-efficient ansatz circuit with the COBYLA optimizer. By comparing with the classical Hartree-Fock baseline, it demonstrates VQE's ability to solve molecular energies within chemical accuracy.",
